# "end" is used in two senses in S3: an end to be effected (a purpose to bring about) and an independently existing end (the rational being). The text draws this distinction itself and keeps each claim in a single sense throughout.
# A1 passes from "not an end to be effected" to "an independently existing end". These are two different claims, each in its own sense of "end", so A1 is not a bridge between senses of one word.
